    {
      "id": "e6a75d4d173354e3084bb0795cc97d20f19fad66",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2558636326,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Nice, but what about SUPI not containing an IMSI but a NAI instead (that can be used for non 3GPP)?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-12T11:52:36.133Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-12T17:14:42.578Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 390614354,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20177,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2559024573,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Nothing will be done since it will not match the regex. Did you have something on your mind that could be done? I can't see how NAI can be used to map to IMSI.\n\n```\nTS23.003\n28.7.2\tNAI format for SUPI\nThe NAI for SUPI shall have the form username@realm as specified in clause 2.2 of IETF RFC 7542 [126].\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6524193,
            "username": "oakimk",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Joakim Karlsson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6524193/avatar.png?v=1787702414",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/oakimk"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-12T14:26:34.887Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-12T17:14:42.578Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 390614354,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20177,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2559388376,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "My comment was actually done without really checking the code as I was on my phone. I first assumed it would create a new filter specific to NF interfaces to find related packets (and in this context a NAI would have been useful )but I just spotted the add_assoc_imsi_item() API call that is IMSI specific so you can disregard my comment.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-12T17:05:17.740Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-12T17:14:42.578Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 390614354,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20177,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2559402099,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Well, yes that is what it actually does. Now you can filter on `e212.assoc.imsi == \"240011111111111\"` and messages where Supi with `imsi-` has been included will be filtered. Together with other protocols like GTPv2, GTPP, PFCP and Diameter.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6524193,
            "username": "oakimk",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Joakim Karlsson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6524193/avatar.png?v=1787702414",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/oakimk"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-12T17:14:42.017Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-12T17:14:42.578Z",
